data.content:
Here are the three breaking changes affecting your code in EF Core 10, with fixes:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

The parameter changed from `Expression<Func<...>>` to `Func<...>`. Your manual expression tree code won't compile.

**Fix** — use the new imperative lambda:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

## 2. Complex type columns are now auto-uniquified

Two changes hit you:

- **Same-level duplicates**: `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` no longer silently share one column — EF appends a number (e.g. `Street1`). Existing migrations will generate an unwanted rename.
- **Nested complex types**: `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` now maps to `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (full path) instead of the old `BillingAddress_City`.

**Fix** — pin explicit column names to preserve your schema:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// For nested complex types, keep the old shorter name:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method gained a `string logCommandText` parameter (for redacted SQL logging).

**Fix** — add the parameter:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← new
    {
        // Use logCommandText (redacted) for logs;
        // use command.CommandText for actual execution.
    }
}
```

Update all other interface methods (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) the same way.
